#: index.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "Zooms the view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Camera View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid "The camera view displays the scene from the camera's point of view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "The camera view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "The blue box displays the field of view when the scene is rendered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "You cannot change control points in the camera view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid "Visibility Levels"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "By default all objects are displayed in the wireframe views."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each object with a wire frame has a visibility level. You can specify a visibility level relative to the parent's visibility level or an absolute value. Objects are only displayed if they are selected or their visibility level is smaller or equal the chosen scene visibility level in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "View Layouts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpovmodeler; comes with a default view layout: The object tree and the object properties view to the left and four graphical views to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you don't like the default layout, or need another layout, you can freely configure it. You can even save multiple view layouts and switch between them on the fly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Modifying the View Layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can move the existing views by dragging the handle on top of the views around while the &Ctrl; key is pressed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "The dock widget handle"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "To dock a widget above or below an existing view, drag the handle to the top or bottom of a view. A rectangle will indicate the new position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "To create a new column, drag the handle to the right or left side of another view. The view will then dock to the left or right side of the view and span the full height."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you want multiple views sharing the same space, drag the handle to the center of another view. You can then switch between the views by clicking the corresponding tab on top of the views."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid "The tabbed view layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid "The last layout possibility are floating views: views that are not docked into the main view. To undock a view, drag the handle to the desktop or press the little arrow in the view handle that points to the top left side."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "To close a view, click the little cross in the handle. To prevent closing, click the little box between the arrow and the cross."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can add additional views to the main window. The <guimenu>View</guimenu> menu contains entries for each type of view. New views will be created as floating windows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saving a View Layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can save the current view layout with <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Save View Layout...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> A dialog opens that lets you select an existing layout or create a new one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can then fine-tune your view layout in the <link linkend=\"configure-view-layout-tab\">settings dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "Switching between View Layouts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can switch to a saved view layout by selecting the entry in the <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>View Layout</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Povray; Interaction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rendering the Scene"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid "Once you have created a scene, you will want to render it. &kpovmodeler; uses &Povray; 3.1g to render the scene, so you need a correct installation of &Povray;. At the time of writing &Povray; 3.5 was released. This version is not supported in the &kpovmodeler; 1.0 version."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid "Go to <ulink url=\"http://www.povray.org\">www.povray.org</ulink> to get a version of &Povray; and for installation instructions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:457
#, no-c-format
msgid "To render the current scene, press the render icon <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"rendericon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> <textobject><phrase>The render icon</phrase></textobject> </inlinemediaobject> in the toolbar, or select the <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Render</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "Render Modes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "A render mode is similar to &Povray;s ini file entries. It specifies the image size and quality levels for rendering. If you would like to render your scene with different qualities and sizes, you can add as many render modes as you need, from quick previews to fullscreen high quality images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid "Render Modes Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid "When you press the render settings icon <inlinemediaobject> <imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"rendersettingsicon.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject> <textobject><phrase>The render settings</phrase></textobject> </inlinemediaobject> in the toolbar or select the <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Render Modes...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu icon, the following dialog opens:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid "The render modes selection dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid "This dialog shows the list of all available render modes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Add</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Adds a default render mode to the list</action>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:503
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Removes the selected render mode</action>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Opens a dialog to edit the selected render mode</action>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Up</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Moves the selected render mode one position up</action>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#. +> trunk
#: index.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid "Down"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
